  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#16031\", \"PowerToys#21003\", \"PowerToys#30342\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before: a hotkey that turns the display off right away while the PC keeps running. Moving the mouse or pressing a key wakes it again. PowerToys has no such shortcut today. Past requests were closed as duplicates of the Quick Display tracker, #1052. Related requests are #28624, #18134, #47488 and #47813. In #18134 the team said it had no plans to build it. The archive offers these workarounds:\\n- Create a Windows shortcut or AutoHotkey script that sends the monitor-off message. For example: powershell (Add-Type '[DllImport(\\\"user32.dll\\\")]public static extern int PostMessage(int hWnd, int hMsg, int wParam, int lParam);' -Name a -Pas)::PostMessage(-1,0x0112,0xF170,2). Assign a hotkey to that shortcut.\\n- Use nircmd.exe with the command \\\"nircmd.exe cmdwait 1000 monitor off\\\".\\n- Use Twinkle Tray, which can turn monitors off from a hotkey.\\nTo support the feature, upvote or comment on #1052. Waking the display may require you to sign in again, depending on your \\\"require sign-in\\\" setting.\"}",
